      "statement": "> **OPP-014 has a strong quantified time-exposure signal: 510 delayed ED-transfer cases in six months, with 335 cases involving the two dominant operational exception classes—ICU/HDU bed waits and interdepartmental disputes. Among patients who eventually transferred, median ED stay before transfer was 51 hours and 30 cases remained ≥96 hours. The evidence does not measure staff labour or current automation, so those remain validation questions rather than fabricated ROI inputs.**\\n\\n**OPP-014-03 = PASS → HIGH TIME-EXPOSURE + COORDINATION-BURDEN SIGNAL**\\n\\n**Next: OPP-014-04 — Direct Operational Evidence / Pain Validation.**",
