      "id": "CP-OPP-012-02",
      "title": "OPP-012-02 — Exception + Human Investigation Reconstruction",
      "status": "PASS",
      "investigation_question": "When a critical laboratory result cannot be successfully communicated and acknowledged through the normal notification path, what human investigation, fallback communication and escalation work is required before the case can close?",
      "tested": "OPP-012-02 — Exception + Human Investigation Reconstruction",
      "found": "> **Fortis Bengaluru evidence establishes a high-volume critical-result notification workflow using telephone, SMS and read-back. Broader closed-loop evidence establishes that failed acknowledgement can create provider-identification, follow-up, escalation and closure work. The exact current Fortis residual workload and system boundary remain unverified.**\\n\\n**OPP-012-02 = PASS → HIGH-CONSEQUENCE EXCEPTION PATH SUPPORTED**\\n\\n**Next: OPP-012-03 — Human Effort / Pain Quantification**",
