      "title": "OPP-012-03 — Human Effort / Pain Quantification",
      "status": "PASS",
      "investigation_question": "How much human effort can be defensibly associated with critical-result notification, failed contact and escalation, without inventing a current Fortis failure rate?",
      "tested": "OPP-012-03 — Human Effort / Pain Quantification",
      "found": "> **The Fortis Bengaluru evidence establishes meaningful critical-result workflow volume, while Indian and multi-hospital research quantifies notification effort and demonstrates that failed communication can create escalation work. Labour savings alone may not be sufficient to support a strong commercial opportunity. The decisive value question is whether unresolved acknowledgement/escalation failures are frequent and consequential enough to justify closed-loop automation.**\\n\\n**OPP-012-03 = PASS → HIGH-CONSEQUENCE / TIME-CRITICAL EFFORT SIGNAL**\\n\\n**Next: OPP-012-04 — Direct Operational Evidence / Pain Validation**",
