      "tested": "OPP-013-03 — Human Effort / Pain Quantification",
      "found": "> **The Nayati study provides a strong measured time-exposure signal: approximately 1,476 urgent requests during the study year and 72 minutes of average delay outside the blood bank, including a 34-minute sample/requisition transport component. The study directly identifies courier availability as a plausible contributor. These figures quantify elapsed workflow exposure, not staff labour. The addressable automation fraction, current system capability and actual ROI remain unknown.**\\n\\n**OPP-013-03 = PASS → HIGH TIME-EXPOSURE SIGNAL**\\n\\n**Next: OPP-013-04 — Direct Operational Evidence / Pain Validation.**",
