      "id": "IN-BMC-001-046",
      "statement": "# \`OPP-01-04.md — Multi-Option Remediation Trade-Off Reconstruction\`\\n\\nThe next checkpoint should reconstruct a scenario where:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nONE SITUATION\\n      ↓\\nMULTIPLE VALID REMEDIATIONS\\n      ↓\\nOPTION A\\nOPTION B\\nOPTION C\\n      ↓\\nTRADE-OFFS\\n      ↓\\nRISK\\n+\\nIMPACT\\n+\\nDEPENDENCIES\\n+\\nREVERSIBILITY\\n+\\nCURRENT STATE\\n      ↓\\nDECISION\\n      ↓\\nEXECUTION\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nThe key question:\\n\\n> **Does BMC provide a native mechanism for dynamically selecting among multiple viable remediation strategies using contextual trade-offs, or does it primarily expose policy-matched automation choices for human or predefined automatic execution?**\\n\\nThis is the next meaningful test.\\n\\n---",
      "basis": [
        "EV-BMC-001-042",
        "EV-BMC-001-043"
      ],
      "implication": "# \`OPP-01-04.md — Multi-Option Remediation Trade-Off Reconstruction\`\\n\\nThe next checkpoint should reconstruct a scenario where:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nONE SITUATION\\n      ↓\\nMULTIPLE VALID REMEDIATIONS\\n      ↓\\nOPTION A\\nOPTION B\\nOPTION C\\n      ↓\\nTRADE-OFFS\\n      ↓\\nRISK\\n+\\nIMPACT\\n+\\nDEPENDENCIES\\n+\\nREVERSIBILITY\\n+\\nCURRENT STATE\\n      ↓\\nDECISION\\n      ↓\\nEXECUTION\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nThe key question:\\n\\n> **Does BMC provide a native mechanism for dynamically selecting among multiple viable remediation strategies using contextual trade-offs, or does it primarily expose policy-matched automation choices for human or predefined automatic execution?**\\n\\nThis is the next meaningful test.\\n\\n---",
