      "id": "IN-BMC-001-050",
      "statement": "# 12. Proposed Trade-Off Reconstruction\\n\\nConsider a hypothetical operational situation:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nSITUATION\\nDatabase service degraded\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nThree valid actions exist:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nA — Restart affected service\\nB — Fail over to secondary\\nC — Scale / redistribute workload\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nEach has different consequences.\\n\\n| Action | Speed | Risk | Blast radius | Reversibility | Dependency |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| A | High | Medium | Low | High | Low |\\n| B | Medium | High | High | Medium | Medium |\\n| C | Medium | Low | Medium | High | High |\\n\\nA true trade-off engine would need to evaluate the live situation and choose.\\n\\nThe important point:\\n\\n> **This table is an experimental reconstruction, not a documented BMC workflow.**\\n\\n---",
