      "id": "EV-BMC-002-006",
      "statement": "# 1. Research Question\\n\\nOPP-02-02 established direct evidence that BMC service requests can enter genuine exception states:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nREQUEST\\n ↓\\nFULFILLMENT\\n ↓\\nFAILURE\\n ↓\\nFAULT\\n ↓\\nERROR DETAILS\\n ↓\\nRECOVERY\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nBMC also provides restart eligibility rules and multiple approval outcomes.\\n\\nThe next question is narrower:\\n\\n> **When fulfillment fails and more than one recovery path could potentially be appropriate, what decision criteria determine the next path, and does BMC dynamically select that path or mainly execute predefined workflow branches?**\\n\\nThe target decision is:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nFULFILLMENT FAILURE\\n        ↓\\nUNDERSTAND FAILURE\\n        ↓\\nAVAILABLE RECOVERY PATHS\\n        ↓\\nDECISION CRITERIA\\n        ↓\\nSELECT\\n        ↓\\nEXECUTE\\n        ↓\\nVERIFY\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n---",
