      "id": "IN-BMC-002-001",
      "statement": "### Selection Rationale\\n\\nOPP-01 was closed after repeated testing showed that incident/remediation automation was already too mature and too broadly implemented across BMC's portfolio.\\n\\nOPP-02 therefore deliberately moves to a different business decision domain:\\n\\n> **Service-request fulfillment and exception handling**\\n\\nThis domain was selected because the public BMC evidence shows a dense automation surface around:\\n\\n- service-request definitions;\\n- approval criteria;\\n- automated fulfillment;\\n- workflow/process definitions;\\n- request states;\\n- fulfillment exceptions;\\n- routing;\\n- integrations;\\n- human approval;\\n- policy-driven execution.\\n\\nBMC's own glossary defines a Service Request Definition (SRD) as containing criteria for approvals and service-level management as well as a process definition supporting automated service delivery.\\n\\nThe objective is therefore not to prove that BMC can automate service requests.\\n\\nIt clearly can.\\n\\nThe objective is to discover whether **exceptions inside otherwise automated fulfillment create independent decision/automation opportunities**.\\n\\n---",
      "basis": [
        "CL-BMC-002-001",
        "EV-BMC-002-001",
        "EV-BMC-002-002",
        "EV-BMC-002-003",
        "EV-BMC-002-004",
        "EV-BMC-002-005"
      ],
