      "id": "IN-BMC-002-009",
      "statement": "# \`OPP-02-02.md — Real Service-Request Exception Reconstruction\`\\n\\nThe next checkpoint should reconstruct the **closest evidence-backed real-world exception scenario**.\\n\\nIt should answer:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nWHAT GOES WRONG?\\n        ↓\\nWHO DECIDES?\\n        ↓\\nWHAT INFORMATION IS USED?\\n        ↓\\nWHAT OPTIONS EXIST?\\n        ↓\\nWHAT IS AUTOMATED?\\n        ↓\\nWHAT REQUIRES HUMAN JUDGMENT?\\n        ↓\\nWHAT HAPPENS AFTER THE DECISION?\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nWe should specifically search for evidence around:\\n\\n- fulfillment failures;\\n- approval exceptions;\\n- unavailable services;\\n- request corrections;\\n- SLA-risk requests;\\n- alternative fulfillment;\\n- manual exception handling;\\n- recurring exceptions converted into automation.\\n\\nIf the evidence shows BMC already handles the exception intelligently enough, **kill this opportunity quickly**.\\n\\nIf the evidence reveals a recurring decision surface, then OPP-02 can split into multiple independent automation opportunities.\\n\\n---",
      "basis": [
        "CL-BMC-002-001",
        "EV-BMC-002-001",
        "EV-BMC-002-002",
        "EV-BMC-002-003",
        "EV-BMC-002-004",
        "EV-BMC-002-005"
      ],
