  "primary_question": "OPP-03-01 identified a strong real-world workload: BMC describes a large Asia/Pacific bank managing **hundreds of job-scheduling change requests daily**, with manual creation and status checking in BMC Helix ITSM. BMC's Control-M Workload Change Manager integration was positioned to automate that administrative interaction.\\n\\nThe question now is:\\n\\n> What is the actual change decision, what evidence informs it, what does BMC already automate, and where does human judgment remain?\\n\\nThis is deliberately different from asking whether change management is automated.\\n\\n---",
