      "id": "IN-BMC-003-002",
      "statement": "## 9. Decision #4 — Does the collision actually matter?\\n\\nBMC explicitly states that colliding changes can coexist when the change coordinator or manager determines that the changes do not actually conflict—for example, when one implementation will not impede or undo the other.\\n\\nTherefore:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nCOLLISION DETECTED\\n        ↓\\nDO THEY ACTUALLY CONFLICT?\\n        ↓\\nYES → MANAGE / RESCHEDULE / RESOLVE\\nNO  → IGNORE WITH JUSTIFICATION\\n\`\`\`",
