      "id": "IN-BMC-003-008",
      "statement": "# 3. Collision is not necessarily a true operational conflict\\n\\nThis is the most important finding in the checkpoint.\\n\\nBMC explicitly states that two colliding changes can coexist when the change coordinator or change manager determines that the nature of the changes does not actually create a conflict—for example, when one change will not impede or undo the other.\\n\\nTherefore:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nSYSTEM DETECTS COLLISION\\n        ↓\\nHUMAN INTERPRETS ACTUAL INTERACTION\\n        ↓\\nTRUE CONFLICT?\\n ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐\\n YES                         NO\\n ↓                            ↓\\nMANAGE / CHANGE             IGNORE\\nSCHEDULE                     +\\n                             JUSTIFICATION\\n\`\`\`",
