      "id": "EV-BMC-004-023",
      "statement": "# 4. The strongest BMC-specific evidence is actually the workflow engine underneath the task\\n\\nBMC documents a general approval architecture that can be attached to cases and tasks.\\n\\nFor cases, approval logic can include:\\n\\n- self-approval;\\n- approval flows;\\n- chains of approvals;\\n- expressions determining which approval applies;\\n- approval outcomes that determine the next case status.\\n\\n\\n\\nFor tasks, BMC similarly supports:\\n\\n- self-approval;\\n- approval flows;\\n- approval chains;\\n- approver qualification expressions;\\n- status transitions after approval/rejection;\\n- automatic approval of tasks that meet defined expressions.\\n\\n\\n\\nThis gives us a much stronger implementation pattern than the undocumented internal logic of the invoice task.\\n\\n---",
      "classification": "SOURCE_EVIDENCE",
      "source": "SRC-FILE-BMC-004-03",
