      "id": "IN-BMC-004-004",
      "statement": "# 7. Why this is a high-value research domain even before an ART opportunity exists\\n\\nAccounts payable is not a single decision.\\n\\nA realistic enterprise invoice workflow can contain multiple decision surfaces:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nINVOICE\\n ↓\\nIS IT VALID?\\n ↓\\nIS THE VENDOR VALID?\\n ↓\\nIS THE AMOUNT CORRECT?\\n ↓\\nDOES IT MATCH SUPPORTING DATA?\\n ↓\\nIS APPROVAL REQUIRED?\\n ↓\\nWHO SHOULD APPROVE?\\n ↓\\nIS PAYMENT AUTHORIZED?\\n ↓\\nWHEN SHOULD PAYMENT OCCUR?\\n ↓\\nHAS PAYMENT ACTUALLY SETTLED?\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nThe BMC content package establishes the existence of the core invoice workflow, but **does not by itself establish every one of these specific controls**.\\n\\nTherefore these are research hypotheses, not facts.\\n\\n---",
