      "id": "IN-BMC-004-057",
      "statement": "# 1. Research objective\\n\\nOPP-04-03 established that BMC publicly documents the **Review Invoice** task but does not expose its invoice-specific validation expressions.\\n\\nThis checkpoint therefore asks:\\n\\n> **What happens when a business task requires approval, does not qualify for automatic approval, is rejected, has no matching approval route, or encounters an approval error—and how can those patterns be reused by ART?**\\n\\nThe evidence is much stronger here because BMC documents the underlying approval engine in detail.\\n\\nThe key distinction remains:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nINVOICE-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\\n        ≠\\nGENERIC BMC APPROVAL ENGINE\\n        ≠\\nART-DERIVED WORKFLOW PATTERN\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n---",
      "basis": [
        "EV-BMC-004-026",
        "EV-BMC-004-027",
        "EV-BMC-004-028"
      ],
      "implication": "# 1. Research objective\\n\\nOPP-04-03 established that BMC publicly documents the **Review Invoice** task but does not expose its invoice-specific validation expressions.\\n\\nThis checkpoint therefore asks:\\n\\n> **What happens when a business task requires approval, does not qualify for automatic approval, is rejected, has no matching approval route, or encounters an approval error—and how can those patterns be reused by ART?**\\n\\nThe evidence is much stronger here because BMC documents the underlying approval engine in detail.\\n\\nThe key distinction remains:\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nINVOICE-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION\\n        ≠\\nGENERIC BMC APPROVAL ENGINE\\n        ≠\\nART-DERIVED WORKFLOW PATTERN\\n\`\`\`\\n\\n---",
