      "id": "IN-BMC-004-083",
      "statement": "# Research Integrity Note\\n\\nThis checkpoint found **real BMC implementation mechanisms**, but it did not pretend that those mechanisms are necessarily configured inside the Sample Finance Received Invoice workflow.\\n\\nThe strongest evidence-supported conclusion is:\\n\\n> **BMC has a mature exception-and-approval execution architecture that can support the Received Invoice workflow, but the public documentation does not expose the exact invoice-specific approval and exception configuration.**\\n\\nThat distinction should remain explicit in ART's intelligence repository.\\n\\nThe next research should therefore focus on **actual automation and integration wiring**, where we may uncover concrete implementation strategies that can be reused across companies.",
