      "statement": "### Still unknown\\n\\n\`\`\`text\\nINVOICE VALIDATION RULES\\nPO MATCHING\\nDUPLICATE DETECTION\\nVENDOR VALIDATION\\nTAX VALIDATION\\nPAYMENT TERMS\\nERP INTEGRATION\\nINVOICE-SPECIFIC APPROVAL THRESHOLDS\\nINVOICE-SPECIFIC EXCEPTION LOGIC\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nTherefore the most valuable conclusion is not an opportunity verdict.\\n\\nIt is this:\\n\\n> **BMC's enterprise workflow architecture separates qualification, automation, human governance, approval routing, decision quorum, state transition and auditability. That architecture is reusable ART implementation intelligence even though the exact invoice-review rules remain undisclosed.**\\n\\nThe next checkpoint should therefore go directly into the **exception and approval paths**, where we have a much better chance of uncovering concrete decision logic.",
