      "investigation_question": "## Company\\nServiceNow\\n## Opportunity\\nOPP-006\\n## Checkpoint\\nOPP-006-01\\n## Investigation Type\\n**New business decision domain discovery**\\n## Status",
      "tested": "**New business decision domain discovery**",
      "found": "OPP-005 was killed after testing Major Incident Management.\\nOPP-006 therefore starts from a different business workflow:\\n> **Field Service Management — exception-driven work allocation and service recovery.**\\nThis is deliberately not an extension of major-incident management.\\nThe initial domain is:\\nCUSTOMER / SERVICE REQUEST\\n↓\\nFIELD WORK ORDER\\n↓\\nTECHNICIAN / CREW / PARTS / LOCATION\\n↓\\nSCHEDULE\\n↓\\nFIELD EXECUTION\\n↓\\nEXCEPTION\\n↓\\nRE-ALLOCATION / RESCHEDULING / RECOVERY\\nThe objective is **not** to claim that ServiceNow has a Field Service gap.\\nThe objective is to determine whether there is a specific consequential decision inside field-service exceptions that survives ServiceNow's current native capabilities.",
